{
  "id": "changes",
  "title": "Bug-introducing changes (before/after pairs)",
  "description": "Hand-written pairs in the spirit of Signal65's bug-introducing-commit method: each case is one plausible edit, 'before' is the correct code and 'after' is the same file once the edit has introduced one defect. A scanner should flag the after tree at the labelled lines and stay quiet on the before tree; any finding on a before tree is a false positive. The edits were written to look like ordinary refactors, not shaped to the rules, so several are expected misses.",
